@@ -2,4 +2,24 @@
 
 Runs lint, tests, and a scheduled CodeQL analysis.
 
-Actions are referenced by major version tag. There is no Dependabot configuration.
+## Action updates
+
+Every action in `.github/workflows/` is pinned to a full commit SHA, with the
+release it corresponds to in a trailing comment (for example
+`actions/checkout@<sha> # v7.0.1`). Tags are mutable, so they are not used.
+
+Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) maintains these pins:
+
+- It checks the `github-actions` ecosystem weekly.
+- All action updates are grouped into a single pull request.
+- A 7-day cooldown skips releases that are less than a week old, so a
+  compromised release has time to be noticed and withdrawn.
+- It rewrites both the SHA and the version comment.
+
+Review each update pull request by reading the upstream diff between the old
+and new SHA, not just the version number, and merge it promptly. SHA-pinned
+actions may not raise security alerts, so these pull requests are the update
+path.
+
+When adding a new action, pin it to the SHA of its latest release and keep the
+version comment, so Dependabot can maintain it.
